  "background": "folk_hero",
  "backstory": "He was found amidst the smoldering ruins of a mountain caravan, a nameless babe with the blood of two worlds warring in his veins. Raised on the fringes of a nervous border-town, he was always a creature of the periphery, never truly welcomed until the night the Frost-Grave dead rose from their barrows. While the local militia faltered in the suffocating dark, he stepped into the fray, his darkvision cutting through the unnatural fog as if it were midday. With a savage, rhythmic brutality and a presence so menacing it seemed to chill the very air, he broke the siege single-handedly. He fell a dozen times and rose a dozen more, his relentless endurance turning a certain massacre into a miraculous victory. By sunrise, the town was saved, and though the villagers offered him a place at their hearths, he remained a stranger—a hero with no name, known only by the trail of splintered bone he left behind in the snow.\n\nThe wild became his sanctuary and his chapel, for only in the untamed reaches could a soul such as his find a reflection of its own restless nature. He embraced the path of the ranger, turning his survival instincts into a disciplined craft of tracking, trapping, and monster-slaying. He wanders the jagged edges of the map, driven by a silent, unshakable bond to protect the innocent from the horrors that dwell in the deep woods. His greatest flaw is the isolation he nurtures like a wound; he fears that if he ever accepts a name or a home, his savage edge will dull and he will fail when the next great darkness emerges. Thus, he remains a ghost of the frontier, a nameless guardian who expects no gratitude, seeking only the next hunt to justify the relentless fire that burns within his breast.",
